# =============================================================================
# G WORLD — static host routing rules (Cloudflare Pages)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom; the first match wins.
#
# What is deliberately NOT in this file: the clean-URL rewrites that a host
# without built-in HTML handling would need (`/browse  /browse.html  200`).
# Pages already does that itself, and `200` rewrites fight it:
#
#   /browse            → the rule rewrites internally to /browse.html
#   /browse.html       → Pages strips the extension: 308 → /browse
#   /browse            → matches the rule again … an infinite redirect loop
#
# Cloudflare says exactly that when it parses such a file:
#
#   ▲ Found 1 invalid redirect rule: Infinite loop detected in this rule and has
#     been ignored. This will cause a redirect to strip `.html` or `/index` and
#     end up triggering this rule again.
#       at public/_redirects:10 | /                /index.html                          200
#
# With those rules gone, Pages serves `/browse` from `browse.html` (200, address
# bar unchanged), `/browse.html` redirects once to the clean URL, `/` serves
# `index.html` and `/admin/students` serves `admin/students.html`. Untouched
# paths fall through to Pages itself, which answers with `404.html`.
#
# Only redirects that Pages cannot infer belong here — the short links people
# type or paste, pointing straight at the clean URL so a browser makes one hop.
# =============================================================================

# Short links people actually type or paste.
/verify/:code    /verify?code=:code             302
/q/:code         /verify?code=:code             302
/enrol/:slug     /course?slug=:slug             302
/learn/:lesson   /lesson?id=:lesson             302
/course/:slug    /course?slug=:slug             302
/lesson/:id      /lesson?id=:id                 302
